    "description": "The public TelemetryClient constructor currently requires an endpoint and project key, and released clients also need optional credentials, request timeouts, retry counts, tracing exporters, and keep-alive settings. The endpoint and project must remain positional, but new optional settings will be added every few releases. Existing callers must continue compiling unchanged, and the library must distinguish an omitted boolean or zero-valued setting from an explicit false or zero. Callers should be able to combine only the settings they care about, with later overrides replacing earlier ones. The resulting client must use an immutable configuration snapshot so a caller cannot mutate settings after construction. Passing a mutable configuration record is undesirable because tenants commonly retain it, while repeatedly expanding the constructor would break source compatibility. The decision is specifically how optional constructor settings are represented and applied while the required parameters and existing call sites remain stable.",
    "decision_statement": "Choose how optional client settings are supplied as named, composable overrides over defaults without changing the required constructor signature or exposing mutable configuration.",
    "notes": "functional-options fits named composable overrides over defaults with a stable required signature and immutable snapshot; builder is the near miss for stepwise optional configuration."
